NAME
       last - list recent logins and reboots (also lastb, failed logins)

SYNOPSIS
       last
       lastb

DESCRIPTION
       last reads /var/log/wtmp and lists who logged in, from where (the
       terminal and, for ssh, the remote host), when, and for how long,
       newest first. "still logged in" marks sessions that are open now. The
       reboot lines show each boot, with the kernel version. The last line
       says when the file starts.

       lastb shows failed login attempts from /var/log/btmp, and only root
       may run it. Many failures for one account can mean someone is
       guessing passwords.

EXAMPLES
           last
           last | grep student

FILES
       /var/log/wtmp, /var/log/btmp

SEE ALSO
       lastlog(8), who(1), w(1), journalctl(1)
